WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
Let's make A pocket-sized snow village.

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:07.951
Mould little snow houses with reusable cups, connect them with paths and invent the

3
00:00:07.951 --> 00:00:08.305
residents.

4
00:00:08.685 --> 00:00:11.500
No tunnels or climbable structures.

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.960
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.070
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.695
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:20.075 --> 00:00:23.845
An adult chooses a safe snow area and supervises weather breaks.

9
00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:30.544
Keep structures miniature and solid; no digging tunnels, hollow shelters or roofs people could

10
00:00:30.544 --> 00:00:30.995
enter.

11
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.690
Step 1.

12
00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.930
Plan a small neighbourhood.

13
00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:41.105
On flat snow, mark a patch about 50 centimetres across with the blunt twig.

14
00:00:41.485 --> 00:00:44.025
Draw where two houses and a path will go.

15
00:00:44.405 --> 00:00:47.070
Leave space to walk around the village.

16
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.830
Grown-up help.

17
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.105
Check the area and clothing.

18
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.680
Step 2.

19
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:55.735
Pack the first mould.

20
00:00:56.115 --> 00:01:00.620
Fill a cup with packable snow, pressing each small handful down with a mitten.

21
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.310
Level the top.

22
00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:06.785
If the snow will not pack, use a flat relief picture instead.

23
00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:08.545
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:10.745
Help test the snow.

25
00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.512
Step 3.

26
00:01:13.892 --> 00:01:15.722
Turn out two houses.

27
00:01:16.102 --> 00:01:19.297
Turn the cup upside down onto the planned spot.

28
00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:21.837
Tap gently and lift it straight up.

29
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:24.557
Make a second house with the other cup.

30
00:01:24.937 --> 00:01:26.757
Keep both solid and low.

31
00:01:27.137 --> 00:01:28.517
Grown-up help.

32
00:01:28.897 --> 00:01:31.947
Help release a stuck mould without forcing it.

33
00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.484
Step 4.

34
00:01:34.864 --> 00:01:36.249
Connect the village.

35
00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:40.369
Use the blunt twig to trace a shallow path between houses.

36
00:01:40.749 --> 00:01:45.534
Press a door and window shape onto each surface without hollowing out the buildings.

37
00:01:45.914 --> 00:01:48.414
Add a small snow courtyard if you like.

38
00:01:48.794 --> 00:01:50.174
Grown-up help.

39
00:01:50.554 --> 00:01:53.564
Keep the markings shallow and structures solid.

40
00:01:55.001 --> 00:01:56.176
Step 5.

41
00:01:56.556 --> 00:01:58.291
Tell the winter story.

42
00:01:58.671 --> 00:02:01.381
Give the village a name and invent its residents.

43
00:02:01.761 --> 00:02:06.426
Gather the cups and twig, check the area for anything left behind, and take

44
00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.426
a warm-up break.

45
00:02:07.806 --> 00:02:09.186
Grown-up help.

46
00:02:09.566 --> 00:02:12.891
Check everyone is comfortable and collect equipment.

47
00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.249
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

48
00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:21.179
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

49
00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:23.579
Your creation can look different.

50
00:02:23.959 --> 00:02:26.644
Retrieve every tool and added material.

51
00:02:27.024 --> 00:02:30.924
Leave only snow where permitted and expect it to change with the weather.

52
00:02:31.304 --> 00:02:32.294
Well done.

53
00:02:32.674 --> 00:02:35.104
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

